# Project Overview

Inventory and sales management app for a solo-owner clothing shop. The owner
imports clothing bundles from abroad, tracks arrivals and transit loss, manages
individual item pricing, records sales, and views monthly financial reports.

## Stack

- **Frontend:** React 18 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, React Router v6, Vite
- **Backend:** Node.js + TypeScript, Fastify, REST API
- **Database:** SQLite via Prisma ORM (`shop.db`)
- **Host:** Android (Termux) — the built frontend is served as static files by Fastify on port 3000

## Repo Structure

```
project-root/
├── client/          # Vite + React frontend
│   └── src/
│       ├── pages/
│       ├── components/
│       └── lib/
├── server/          # Fastify backend
│   └── src/
│       ├── routes/
│       ├── services/
│       └── prisma/
├── shared/
│   └── types.ts     # Shared TypeScript interfaces — source of truth
├── prisma/
│   └── schema.prisma
└── shop.db
```

## Dev Commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `npm run dev` | Start both client (Vite, port 5173) and server (tsx watch, port 3000) |
| `npm run build` | Vite build → `client/dist/`, which Fastify serves |
| `npm run typecheck` | TypeScript check across client + server + shared |
| `npm run lint` | ESLint across all packages |
| `npx prisma migrate dev` | Apply schema changes and regenerate Prisma client |
| `npx prisma generate` | Regenerate Prisma client without migrating |
| `npx prisma studio` | Open visual DB browser at localhost:5555 |

## Definition of Done

A task is complete when:
1. `npm run build` exits 0
2. `npm run typecheck` reports no errors
3. `npm run lint` reports no warnings
4. The feature works on a 390px-wide screen (Android primary client)


