# Coding Standards

## TypeScript

- Strict mode is on. No `any`. No `@ts-ignore`. No `@ts-expect-error`.
- Use types from `shared/types.ts` wherever they exist. Do not redefine them locally.
- When adding a new shared type, add it to `shared/types.ts` — not inline in a route or component.
- `async/await` only. No `.then()` chains.
- Always type function return values explicitly on service functions and route handlers.

## Backend (Fastify + Prisma)

- Business logic belongs in `server/src/services/`. Route handlers call service functions — they
  do not contain logic themselves. A route handler should be ≤ 20 lines.
- DB access is **only** via the Prisma client. No raw SQL unless Prisma cannot express the query,
  and even then, ask first.
- Prisma `$transaction` is required any time two or more DB writes must succeed or fail together.
  Never do sequential `await prisma.x.create()` + `await prisma.y.create()` for atomic operations.
- Return appropriate HTTP status codes: 200 for reads, 201 for creates, 422 for business-rule
  violations (floor price block, invalid state transitions), 404 for missing records, 400 for
  malformed input.
- Never update `schema.prisma` without explicit instruction from the user.
- Never run `prisma migrate reset` without explicit instruction from the user.

## Frontend (React + Vite)

- Mobile-first. All UI must be usable at 390px width. No horizontal scroll on small screens.
  Use responsive Tailwind classes (`sm:`, `md:`) to enhance for larger screens, not to fix mobile.
- Use shadcn/ui primitives (Table, Dialog, Form, Select, Badge) — do not roll bespoke UI for
  things shadcn already covers.
- Tailwind utility classes only. No custom CSS files. No inline `style=` except for truly
  dynamic values that Tailwind cannot express.
- Keep components small and single-purpose. If a component exceeds ~150 lines, split it.
- No `console.log` in committed code.

## API Conventions

- All endpoints are under `/api/`.
- REST resource naming: `/api/orders`, `/api/orders/:id`, `/api/orders/:id/bundles`, etc.
- Request and response bodies are JSON.
- Validation errors return `{ error: string }`. Business-rule blocks return `{ error: string, code: string }`.

## Dependencies

- Do not install new npm packages without asking the user first.
- Prefer packages already in `package.json`. If something new is genuinely needed, propose it
  and wait for approval before running `npm install`.

## What Never to Do

- Touch `schema.prisma` without being asked
- Run `prisma migrate reset`
- Divide `transportation_fee` into item costs
- Set `cost_price` on InventoryItem to anything other than `Bundle.cost_per_item` at creation time
- Modify `loss_value`, `loss_date`, or `loss_type` on an existing LossEntry
- Apply a recovery in the month the loss occurred instead of the month the recovery occurred


